INTERPRETATION
For every Q>=1, Lemma 5A8H28U gives the unbounded factorization

  E(z)=E_F(z)/(1-z-z^2)^L,
  L=floor((K-1)/Q),
  E_F>=0 coefficientwise.

The safe-Fibonacci residual has no negative coefficient in the displayed
audit.  The first Q>=2 transformed-current negative is -1516, so
coefficientwise positivity after division by the scalar reserve is false;
the residual factor E_F remains necessary.  Proposition 5A8H28V proves
that its degree-five obstruction persists for every prefix j>=5 and
forces scalar-safe head depth at least 2j-6.

Lemma 5A8H28UA gives the unbounded two-Green factorization

  E(z)=F_-(z) C_(K,Q)(z) F_+(z),
  C_(K,Q)>=0 coefficientwise.

The audit formally divides E by F_-F_+ and finds no negative residual
among 11,130 exact coefficients.  This bounded line checks the
implementation; the marked-loop bijection proves the factorization.
The transformed current is nevertheless negative at the exact Q>=2
witness above, with value -411.  The stronger common multibacktrack
reserve also fails there, with value -1228.  Hence the residual crossing
core C_(K,Q) remains load-bearing.

The core-length suffix audit checks 1,610,175 exact coordinates and finds
118 negatives.  Its first negative is the Proposition 5A8H28W witness
at (k,q,j,t,r)=(38,18,25,11,21).  Thus scalar outside-in ordering by
E_F core length is also false: a global allocation must retain core
shape or an equivalent reflected shell/crossing state.

